  "notes": "4-channel compressor/limiter/gate (19\" rack, IEC mains). Per channel: balanced inputs and outputs on XLR and 6.35 mm TRS (the two output connectors are wired in parallel). The quick start guide lists no sidechain jacks for this model. OPERATING LEVEL switch: -10 dBV or +4 dBu. XLR genders follow the usual convention (not stated). Controls from the Quick Start Guide, 'Controls' (1-32), per channel: expander/gate (TRIGGER, RELEASE short/long, GATE), compressor (THRESHOLD, RATIO, LO CONTOUR, INTERACT KNEE, AUTO), OUTPUT (+/-20 dB), IN/OUT METER, IN/OUT (hard bypass), ENHANCER (the guide also calls the enhancer adjustable; whether it has a level knob is not stated), LIMITER (fully right = off), OPERATING LEVEL (+4 dBu / -10 dBV, rear) and COUPLE (stereo link). The guide describes one channel; all channels are taken to be identical. Start positions are app defaults.",
